  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Facilitating access to essential services for survivors of Gender Based Violence in Lesotho</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will provide outreach in most of the districts of Lesotho in order to bring services for survivors of Gender Based Violence to the places where they live.  It will also sensitise survivors to the availability of those services as well as offering practical lessons and guidance by experts.  Most services are centred on the capital, Maseru.  The project will make expert service provision more visible and available around the rest of Lesotho, a country where around 80% of women report having been subjected to Gender Based Violence.</narrative>
  </description>
